        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Actium</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">2 September 31 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a> outside the straits of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambracian-gulf">Ambracian Gulf</a>, near Actium in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">Octavian, with the fleet led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-vipsanius-agrippa">Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa</a>, against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra</a>; 400 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> against 250 larger ones on the morning, and an estimate of 260 against about 140</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Antony</a>'s fleet was routed, Antony and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra</a> escaped with a few ships, the ships left behind were captured or sunk, and Antony's land army deserted or surrendered.</span></div>
